      "text": "It would allow the doctor to commute to the mainland, reducing his need to live on the island.",  
      "why_wrong": "The text never suggests the doctor would move or commute; in fact, it implies he stays because his role is tied to the island. The idea that he would leave is unsupported and contradicts the implication that his job is essential to island life."  
    },  
    {  
      "text": "It would bring more tourists, increasing the demand for medical care and making his job more essential.",  
      "why_wrong": "This reverses the logic of the text. The passage states the bridge could make local services like the doctor’s post 'unnecessary to maintain locally,' not more vital. The increase in visitors is cited by Lund, not Rask, and is not linked to higher medical demand."  
    },  
    {  
      "text": "It would reduce ferry cancellations, making it easier for the doctor to travel to the mainland for training.",  
      "why_wrong": "The text does not mention the doctor needing training or traveling for professional development. The focus is on the bridge making local services redundant, not improving access for professionals. This distractor misrepresents the doctor’s role and the purpose of the bridge."  
    }  
  ]  
